ents per run.\"),\n       row(\"child shares parent budget\",\"enforced\",LS(\"app/tools/documents.py\",\"return await deps.extractor.extract\"),\"Extractor receives the parent run's budget object.\"),\n       row(\"child model usage charged\",\"enforced\",LS(X,\"budget.charge_model(self.settings.extractor_model_id\"),\"Child model usage is charged to the shared budget.\"),\n       row(\"child steps counted\",\"enforced\",LS(X,\"budget.check_step()\"),\"Child turns increment the shared step counter.\"),\n       row(\"child tool calls counted\",\"enforced\",LS(X,\"budget.check_tool_call()\"),\"Child tool calls count against the shared rate.\")])\ncheck(\"B07.4\",\"no\",LS(B,\"if spent > limit:\"),\"Daily spend quotas are only added after a model call has already happened, and BudgetExceeded is raised inside the transaction so the over-limit spend is rolled back and never recorded. Runs may start while a quota is already exhausted (reserve_run_start checks only run-start counts). Tool-call rate has no per-tenant or fleet quota, and count_tokens calls are not charged.\")\n# ---- B08\ncheck(\"B08.1\",\"no\",LS(\"deploy/k8s/networkpolicy.yaml\",\"cidr: 0.0.0.0/0\"),\"A default-deny policy exists, but the last egress rule allows 0.0.0.0/0 (except private ranges) on 443. The ERP rule also selects a whole namespace with no podSelector.\")\ncheck(\"B08.2\",\"unknown\",LS(\"deploy/k8s/networkpolicy.yaml\",\"- 169.254.0.0/16\"),\"Metadata and RFC1918 are excepted from the 0.0.0.0/0 rule, so metadata is blocked. Not excepted: 100.64.0.0/10 and non-RFC1918 internal ranges. Cluster addressing is outside this repo, so I cannot tell whether those reach internal services. No hostNetwork or docker.sock mount in deployment.yaml.\")\ncheck(\"B08.3\",\"yes\",LS(\"deploy/k8s/networkpolicy.yaml\",\"policyTypes: [\\\"Ingress\\\", \\\"Egress\\\"]\"),\"Isolation is defined in NetworkPolicy objects and a separate namespace, not by prompt text.\",\n counter=\"Searched deployment.yaml for hostNetwork, hostPID and docker.sock and found none. gate.py:35 is an operation-name check on erp_call; the ERP scope is enforced by the gateway via the STS scope, so it is not the isolation boundary.\",\n rows=[row(\"default deny\",\"enforced\",LS(\"deploy/k8s/networkpolicy.yaml\",\"policyTypes: [\\\"Ingress\\\", \\\"Egress\\\"]\"),\"podSelector {} with both policy types denies all by default.\"),\n       row(\"named egress peers\",\"enforced\",LS(\"deploy/k8s/networkpolicy.yaml\",\"app: procurement-db\"),\"Database egress names namespace, pod label, and port.\"),\n       row(\"dedicated namespace\",\"enforced\",LS(\"deploy/k8s/deployment.yaml\",\"namespace: procurement-prod\"),\"Agent runs in its own procurement-prod namespace.\"),\n       row(\"no host access\",\"enforced\",LS(\"deploy/k8s/deployment.yaml\",\"automountServiceAccountToken: false\"),\"No hostNetwork, hostPID or docker.sock; token not auto-mounted.\")])\n# ---- B09\ncheck(\"B09.1\",\"no\",LS(\"deploy/k8s/networkpolicy.yaml\",\"cidr: 0.0.0.0/0\"),\"Egress is default-deny, but one rule allows TCP 443 to 0.0.0.0/0 minus private ranges, so the proxy allowlist is not enforced by network policy.\")\ncheck(\"B09.2\",\"no\",LS(\"deploy/k8s/deployment.yaml\",\"value: \\\"http://egress-proxy.egress.svc.cluster.local:3128\\\"\"),\"The proxy is set only by the HTTPS_PROXY env var. The 0.0.0.0/0 rule on 443 lets the pod reach the internet directly. The ipBlock rules are IPv4 only.\")\ncheck(\"B09.3\",\"unknown\",LS(\"app/tools/payments.py\",\"follow_redirects=False\"),\"All four httpx clients disable redirects and use fixed settings URLs; no model-supplied URL fetch tool was found. No resolved-IP check in code, and IPv6 metadata and loopback blocking is not defined in this repo.\")\ncheck(\"B09.4\",\"unknown\",LS(\"deploy/k8s/networkpolicy.yaml\",\"api.anthropic.com\"),\"The proxy allowlist names hosts only, with no account or path limit. api.anthropic.com is a shared service. Proxy config is applied by the platform 