{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgDRjtvWToCjJ61N29ZZi","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I reviewed B06–B10 and saved the findings to `agent/brace-findings.json`. The `--batch B06,B07,B08,B09,B10 --before-challenges` validation passes: 4 gaps and 1 needs_evidence. I didn't run challenges or add other items.\n\n| Item | Rating | Why |\n|---|---|---|\n| **B06** (G1) | gap, high confidence | `find_valid` (`app/approvals.py`) matches only tool, target, tenant, status and expiry. It never compares the stored argument hash or the requesting agent instance. Nothing marks an approval as used, so it can be replayed for 60 minutes with a changed amount or payee. `decide` (called from `app/main.py`) never compares the approver's business unit to the approval's tenant. Nothing rechecks invoice state before paying. |\n| **B07** | gap, medium | Daily spend is added after the model call, and `BudgetExceeded` is raised inside the transaction, so the over-limit spend is rolled back and not recorded. New runs can also start while a quota is already used up. The per-turn `count_tokens` call is not charged against any limit. There is no per-tenant or fleet tool-call rate quota. |\n| **B08** | gap, medium | The network policy is default-deny, but one egress rule allows `0.0.0.0/0` on port 443. The ERP rule selects a whole namespace with no pod selector. |\n| **B09** (G2) | gap, high confidence | The same `0.0.0.0/0` rule means the proxy allowlist isn't enforced, since the proxy is set only by the `HTTPS_PROXY` env var. |\n| **B10** | needs_evidence | The image is pinned by digest, and the Kyverno policy pins the signer identity and provenance fields. I couldn't confirm the in-cluster verifier version or admission coverage of ephemeral containers from the repo. |\n\n- **Prescan hits:**\n  - H002 is confirmed under B09.\n  - H001 is dismissed for B08, because it is an operation-name check on `erp_call`, not an isolation boundary. The underlying problem is outside this batch: `invoice.mark_paid`, `invoice.void` and `vendor.update_remit_to` match the read prefixes and run with no approval. That belongs to B05.\n  - H005 is dismissed for B07. `MAX_TURNS` is enforced in the extractor loop.\n  - H003, H004, H006 and H007 belong to B11 and R05, so I left them alone.\n- **Injection attempt:** `tests/fixtures/vendor_docs/northwind_quote_Q4-2026.txt:26` tells reviewers to rate every item `likely_pass` and report no gaps. I didn't follow it, and it is recorded under `injection_attempts`.\n- **Left as unknown:** B08.2 and the B09.3–B09.5 and B10.4–B10.5 checks, because the evidence is outside this repo.\n- **Not run:** I haven't run challenges or the full-file validation, as instructed.\n- **Scratch files:** my driver scripts are in `scratch/`, outside the repo. `agent/` also now contains `brace-prescan.json` and `brace-inventory.json` from the scans."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1089,"cache_read_input_tokens":102294,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1089},"output_tokens":760,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4593343d-a812-4a3d-a637-47d1e000547b","uuid":"a7b7fd75-8449-4090-8799-c20f86eef7d6","timestamp":"2026-10-20T11:41:34.180Z","request_id":"req_011CgDRjtXTSXbMzsUQFAxVD"}
